7. Risks & Limitations  
- The “up” normal assumes camera Y+ points down; if the camera coordinate convention differs, Z direction may need flipping.  
- RANSAC fit depends on ROI depth density; sparse depth can cause fit failure.  
- Long-edge selection assumes convex ROI and uses consecutive hull edges; extreme skew may select an unintended edge.

8. Reproduction Guide  
1. Build and run `./build/yolo_pose_indemind_left`.  
2. Click four corners of the trampoline bed in the YOLO window.  
3. Confirm “Trampoline Frame: READY” and that hip positions transform into the new frame.
